  "goodToKnow": "Der Komet is a comet: der Halleysche Komet (Halley's Comet), der Kometenschweif (tail). Kometenhaft means meteoric: ein kometenhafter Aufstieg. It's a weak noun: den Kometen. The European Space Agency's Rosetta mission, controlled from Darmstadt, landed the probe Philae on a comet in 2014, a world first. From Greek kometes (long-haired). Plural: die Kometen."
